1
00:06:53,333 --> 00:06:59,333
Can the most famous film star in the world fall for the man on the street?

2
00:13:46,666 --> 00:13:52,666
Notting Hill is a romance, comedy film directed by Roger Michell.

3
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:46,000
London bookstore owner William Thacker's quiet life turns upside down when a chance encounter with famous
actress Anna Scott sparks an unlikely romance challenged by their vastly different worlds.

4
00:27:33,333 --> 00:27:39,333
Anna Scott, played by Julia Roberts.

5
00:34:26,666 --> 00:34:32,666
William Thacker, played by Hugh Grant.

6
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:26,000
Bella, played by Gina McKee.

7
00:48:13,333 --> 00:48:19,333
Max, played by Tim McInnerny.

8
00:55:06,666 --> 00:55:12,666
Spike, played by Rhys Ifans.

9
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
Honey, played by Emma Chambers.

10
01:08:53,333 --> 01:08:59,333
Notting Hill is a 1999 romantic comedy film directed by Roger Michell,
written by Richard Curtis, and produced by Duncan Kenworthy.

11
01:15:46,666 --> 01:15:52,666
It stars Julia Roberts and Hugh Grant, with Rhys Ifans, Emma Chambers, Tim
McInnerny, Gina McKee, and Hugh Bonneville in supporting roles.

12
01:22:40,000 --> 01:22:46,000
The story is of a romance between a British bookshop keeper (Grant) and a famous American actress
(Roberts) who happens to walk into his shop in London's Notting Hill district.

13
01:29:33,333 --> 01:29:39,333
Released on 21 May 1999, Notting Hill was well received by critics and was the
highest-grossing British film of all time upon release, which has since been eclipsed.

14
01:36:26,666 --> 01:36:32,666
At the 57th Golden Globe Awards, the film received three nominations – Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy, Best
Actress – Motion Picture Musical or Comedy (Roberts) and Best Actor – Motion Picture Musical or Comedy (Grant).

15
01:43:20,000 --> 01:43:26,000
It also earned two BAFTA nominations, and won a British
Comedy Award and a Brit Award for its soundtrack.

16
01:50:13,333 --> 01:50:19,333
The film explores themes of new love, london, england,
bookshop, roommates, press conference.

17
01:57:06,666 --> 01:57:12,666
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
